#====================================================================
# PCRE2 draft - Restore Autotools helper execute bits before configure
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-pcre2-autotools-permissions-1913
trigger_tool:           autotools|configure|make|conan
phase:                  configure|build|testing
error_signature:        Permission denied|configure.*cannot execute|config\.guess.*Permission denied|config\.sub.*Permission denied

severity:               2
category:               autotools|conan|ohos-filesystem|execute-permission
match_keywords:         Autotools, configure, config.guess, config.sub, install-sh, missing, chmod, stat.S_IXUSR, OHOS, HMDFS, make check
title:                  Restore Autotools helper execute bits before configure

root_cause:             Autotools helper scripts are executable programs, but some HarmonyOS PC adaptation paths preserve source content without preserving POSIX execute mode bits. The build can fail before compilation even though the generated scripts are otherwise valid.
affected_scope:         Conan recipes for Autotools packages whose source trees include configure, config.guess, config.sub, install-sh, or missing and are built or transferred through OHOS/HMDFS-style paths.
verification_cmd:       Run clean conan create on HarmonyOS PC CI or target runner; require configure to complete, upstream make -j1 check to pass, and Conan test_package to pass with explicit pass rates.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           restore-known-autotools-script-modes
rec_description:        Before configure, walk the recipe, source, and build folders and add owner/group/other execute bits only to known Autotools helper scripts. Then run configure and make check as part of the recipe build.
rec_command:            chmod +x configure config.guess config.sub install-sh missing; ./configure; make -j1; make -j1 check
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      regenerate-autotools-files
fallback_description:   If helper scripts are missing or generated for the wrong project state, regenerate them with the upstream-supported bootstrap/autoreconf flow, then restore execute bits and rerun the full test target.
fallback_command:       autoreconf -fi
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-bootstrap

forbid_1_pattern:       chmod -R \+x
forbid_1_reason:        Making the whole source tree executable hides metadata problems and can package or execute unintended files.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package can gain noisy mode changes and future audits cannot tell which generated scripts actually needed execute bits.

forbid_2_pattern:       make(?!.*check)|pending CI log|pending current CI
forbid_2_reason:        A build-system permission fix changes how upstream scripts execute and must be validated by upstream tests, not only by compilation or placeholder PR text.
forbid_2_consequence:   Reviewers cannot confirm the real upstream test pass rate or whether helper-script execution changed runtime behavior.

principles:             P010, P012
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-pcre2-autotools-permissions-1913.md
last_updated:           2026-08-13
source_event:           pcre2/10.45.1.1 HarmonyOS PC adaptation, issue #1913


authors:                xuguowei
